  "verbalization": "The compound in question, (1R,3R,4S,7S,9S,11S,13R,14R,15R)-4,11,13,14-tetrahydroxy-7-[(2Z,4R)-4-(hydroxymethyl)hex-2-en-2-yl]-3,9,15-trimethoxy-12,12-dimethyl-6,17-dioxabicyclo[11.3.1]heptadecan-5-one, is shown to have a target relationship with LNCaP through multiple pathways. It is identified as a target of two different compounds: Hex-3-en-1-yl 2-methylbut-2-enoate and Lethedioside B. Both of these compounds are themselves targets of LNCaP, suggesting a potential pathway through which the compound may interact with the cell. The evidence suggests that the compound may act through a mechanism involving the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, which is a known target of both Hex-3-en-1-yl 2-methylbut-2-enoate and Lethedioside B. This implies that the compound may exert its effects by modulating the proteasome system, potentially influencing cellular processes in LNCaP cells. The evidence is consistent across different pathways, indicating a possible role in the regulation of LNCaP cell behavior."
